    en: { title: 'Delete X (Twitter) Account Permanently: 30-Day Deactivation Guide', description: 'Delete an X account by using the 30-day deactivation process, download your X archive first, revoke third-party access, and review paid subscriptions.', heading: 'Delete an X account without accidentally reactivating it', overview: 'X uses deactivation as the first step toward permanent account deletion. The account remains recoverable for 30 days, so logging in again during that window reverses the deletion process.', points: ['X states that deactivation starts a 30-day window; if you do not access the account during that period, the account is permanently deleted.', 'Request and download your X data before deactivation if you want an archive. X says the archive should be requested before the account is deactivated.', 'Revoke third-party app access before deactivation because an authorized app can indirectly log in and reactivate the account. Review paid subscriptions separately, especially those purchased through an app store.'] },
